## HQ plotfile consumer / frames drain — eval000118 postmortem + restart

**Old run:** `qball_traj_spiral_v2_t30_hq_eval000118` (deleted, frames t≈13→24.7 lost).
**New run (live):** `qball_traj_spiral_v2_hq_eval000118` (same source `qball_traj_spiral_v2/eval_000118`, fast config, boson_star branch).

### Speedups baked in

| Setting | Default | Override env |
|---|---|---|
| Frame DPI | 90 (was 110) | `GRTECLYN_FRAMES_DPI` |
| Frame buff cap | 512 (was 1024) | `GRTECLYN_FRAMES_BUFF_CAP` |
| Samples per cell | 1 (was 2) | `GRTECLYN_FRAMES_SAMPLES_PER_CELL` |

Net: ~9× faster per plotfile (165s → 18s) at full 11-field HQ set. Exported by `promote_common.sh`, read by `consume_plotfiles/config.py`.

### Why the first restart had wrong frame fields

`promote_common.sh` branches on `GRTRESNA_MATTER_SECTOR` (boson_star → `phi Pi phi_lump0 Pi_lump0`; otherwise → `lump_activity phi_lump_sum`). `run_batch.sh` did not pass it, so it fell through to the wrong branch (fields that don't exist in complex-scalar boson star plotfiles). **Fixed in `run_batch.sh`**: now reads `metadata.json` from the source eval and exports `GRTRESNA_MATTER_SECTOR` / `GRTRESNA_MATTER_MODEL` automatically before launching.

### Code changes (this session)

- `grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/plot/drain_plotfiles_fast.sh` (new)
- `grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/plot/drain_plotfiles_frames.sh` (new)
- `grteclyn-wrapper/src/grteclyn_wrapper/core/plot_consumer.py` — drain/minimal/frames flags
- `grteclyn-wrapper/src/grteclyn_wrapper/core/runner.py` — `drain_plotfile_backlog(frames=None)` default
- `grteclyn-wrapper/.../consume_plotfiles/driver.py` — `spawn` for ProcessPoolExecutor
- `grteclyn-wrapper/.../consume_plotfiles/config.py` — env-overridable `_FRAME_DPI`, `_FRAME_BUFF_CAP`, `_FRAME_SAMPLES_PER_CELL`
- `grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/campaigns/lib/promote_common.sh` — exports fast frame config; boson_star branch
- `grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/campaigns/hq/run_batch.sh` — auto-detect matter sector/model from source eval metadata

