## How to launch drains on existing plotfiles

**Path:**
```bash
export RUN=/home/jovyan/nachevsky/test/simulation/GRTeclyn/runs/grtresna_promote/qball_traj_spiral_v2_hq_eval000118
cd /home/jovyan/nachevsky/test/simulation/GRTeclyn
```

### A) Fast Psi4-only drain (no frames, deletes plotfiles) — DON'T USE on the live run

```bash
CONSUMER_JOBS=2 ./grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/plot/drain_plotfiles_fast.sh "$RUN"
```

### B) Frames drain — full HQ fields, NO geodesic/FTL/projections

```bash
PROJECTION_FIELDS= CONSUMER_JOBS=2 nohup \
  ./grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/plot/drain_plotfiles_frames.sh "$RUN" \
  >> "$RUN/frames_drain.log" 2>&1 &
```

Override field set or rebuild quality: `GRTECLYN_FRAMES_DPI=110 GRTECLYN_FRAMES_BUFF_CAP=1024 GRTECLYN_FRAMES_SAMPLES_PER_CELL=2`.

### C) Direct consumer (full control)

```bash
source grteclyn-wrapper/scripts/lib/env.sh
export GRTECLYN_FRAMES=1 GRTECLYN_CONSUMER_DRAIN=0 GRTECLYN_CONSUMER_DRAIN_MINIMAL=1
export GRTECLYN_PSI4=0 GRTECLYN_EVOLVING_GEODESIC=0
export GRTECLYN_PROJECTION_FIELDS=""
export GRTECLYN_FRAMES_FIELDS="scalar_activity phi Pi phi_lump0 Pi_lump0 chi chi_minus_1 local_speed shift1 rho_req Weyl4_Re Weyl4_Im Weyl4_Mag"
# use runner's drain_plotfile_backlog()
```

